usage: course check [-h] [--root DIR] [--station PATH] [--install DIR] [--source DIR]
                    [--labsrc DIR] [--solutions DIR] [--lab N] [--json]

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --root DIR       niagara-research checkout (default: $NIAGARA_RESEARCH_DIR, then found from cwd)
  --station PATH   station directory, or its config.bog (zipped or plain XML); default:
                   $COURSE_TRAINING_STATION for the labs, $COURSE_REVIEW_STATION for RA1/RA2,
                   $COURSE_CERT_STATION for EXAM
  --install DIR    Niagara install whose modules/ holds the built jars (default:
                   $COURSE_NIAGARA_INSTALL; jar checks SKIP without either)
  --source DIR     Niagara source tree, one directory per module part, e.g. niagara-
                   help/versions/4.15.6.20/source (default: $COURSE_NIAGARA_SOURCE; source checks
                   SKIP without either)
  --labsrc DIR     lab module sources: the Niagara dev home holding training/ and
                   trafficLightDriver/ (default: $COURSE_LAB_SOURCES; lab-source checks SKIP
                   without either)
  --solutions DIR  the participant's module sources as niagara-research keeps them,
                   sources/n4-dev-course/solutions (default: $COURSE_SOLUTIONS; solutions checks
                   SKIP without either)
  --lab N          only this lab (1-11, B; RA1, RA2, EXAM run only when named); repeatable
  --json           machine JSON output
